13
00:00:21,359 --> 00:00:23,420
carry little or no student debt,

14
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:25,675
and often end up owning businesses.

15
00:00:25,855 --> 00:00:28,290
Today, we're going to look at twelve

16
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:31,536
quiet advantages that help tradespeople out earn

17
00:00:31,536 --> 00:00:33,971
many office workers over a lifetime,

18
00:00:33,971 --> 00:00:35,933
and the honest downsides too.

19
00:00:36,282 --> 00:00:39,382
Plumbers and electricians versus office workers.

20
00:00:39,562 --> 00:00:41,264
Twelve quiet advantages,

21
00:00:41,264 --> 00:00:42,894
and the real tradeoffs.

22
00:00:43,244 --> 00:00:44,765
Let's be fair from the start.

23
00:00:44,945 --> 00:00:47,544
This isn't a video saying college is

24
00:00:47,544 --> 00:00:49,926
bad or office jobs are a mistake.

25
00:00:50,106 --> 00:00:52,419
Many office careers pay very well,

26
00:00:52,419 --> 00:00:54,597
and many people are happier at a

27
00:00:54,597 --> 00:00:56,434
desk than in a crawl space.

28
00:00:56,614 --> 00:00:58,549
The point is that the old story,

29
00:00:58,549 --> 00:01:01,209
where hands on work automatically means less

30
00:01:01,209 --> 00:01:03,023
money, is no longer true for a

31
00:01:03,023 --> 00:01:03,870
lot of people.

32
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:04,839
And for some,

33
00:01:04,839 --> 00:01:06,844
the trades may be the faster path

34
00:01:06,844 --> 00:01:07,451
to wealth.

35
00:01:07,801 --> 00:01:10,656
We'll use government data where we can,

36
00:01:10,656 --> 00:01:13,804
mainly from the Bureau of Labor Statistics.

37
00:01:13,984 --> 00:01:15,548
Where we use examples,

38
00:01:15,548 --> 00:01:19,387
they're simplified illustrations to explain the ideas,

39
00:01:19,387 --> 00:01:20,311
not promises.

40
00:01:20,491 --> 00:01:22,807
Pay varies enormously by state,

41
00:01:22,807 --> 00:01:26,469
city, specialty, union membership and experience,

42
00:01:26,469 --> 00:01:29,158
and your results will depend on your

43
00:01:29,158 --> 00:01:29,756
choices.

44
00:01:30,105 --> 00:01:32,437
We'll go through the twelve advantages,

45
00:01:32,437 --> 00:01:34,530
then look at the whole picture from

46
00:01:34,530 --> 00:01:35,307
three angles.

47
00:01:35,487 --> 00:01:38,276
The numbers, meaning a lifetime comparison of

48
00:01:38,276 --> 00:01:38,958
two people.

49
00:01:39,138 --> 00:01:41,859
The psychology, meaning why so many people

50
00:01:41,859 --> 00:01:43,155
overlook the trades.

51
00:01:43,335 --> 00:01:44,560
And the playbook,

52
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:47,585
meaning how someone actually gets started,

53
00:01:47,585 --> 00:01:49,314
at eighteen or at forty.

54
00:01:49,664 --> 00:01:51,789
Let's start with the paycheck itself,

55
00:01:51,789 --> 00:01:54,659
because that's where most people's assumptions are

56
00:01:54,659 --> 00:01:55,922
furthest from reality.

57
00:01:56,272 --> 00:01:58,606
Pay data comes from the Bureau of

58
00:01:58,606 --> 00:02:02,425
Labor Statistics Occupational Outlook Handbook and its

59
00:02:02,425 --> 00:02:05,537
occupational employment and wage statistics.

60
00:02:05,717 --> 00:02:06,649
For May 2023,

61
00:02:06,649 --> 00:02:09,516
the Bureau reported median annual pay of

62
00:02:09,516 --> 00:02:12,742
about sixty one thousand five hundred dollars

63
00:02:12,742 --> 00:02:15,250
for both plumbers and electricians,

64
00:02:15,250 --> 00:02:17,902
compared with a median of about forty

65
00:02:17,902 --> 00:02:20,984
eight thousand dollars for all occupations.

66
00:02:21,164 --> 00:02:23,874
Student debt information comes from the Federal

67
00:02:23,874 --> 00:02:26,180
Reserve and the Department of Education.

68
00:02:26,360 --> 00:02:28,305
This video is education,

69
00:02:28,305 --> 00:02:30,818
not financial or career advice.

70
00:02:31,168 --> 00:02:32,271
Advantage 1.

71
00:02:32,451 --> 00:02:33,926
Pay above the median.

72
00:02:34,106 --> 00:02:36,259
the middle plumber out earns the middle

73
00:02:36,259 --> 00:02:36,590
worker

74
00:02:36,940 --> 00:02:38,218
Advantage one.

75
00:02:38,398 --> 00:02:40,592
Higher pay than many people expect.

76
00:02:40,772 --> 00:02:43,756
According to the Bureau of Labor Statistics,

77
00:02:43,756 --> 00:02:46,808
the median plumber and the median electrician

78
00:02:46,808 --> 00:02:49,589
each earned about sixty one thousand five

79
00:02:49,589 --> 00:02:51,488
hundred dollars in May 2023.

80
00:02:51,668 --> 00:02:54,310
The median for all occupations was about

81
00:02:54,310 --> 00:02:55,697
