125
00:04:29,601 --> 00:04:31,457
Instead of paying tuition,

126
00:04:31,457 --> 00:04:34,455
apprentices earn a wage that usually rises

127
00:04:34,455 --> 00:04:35,882
as they gain skills.

128
00:04:36,233 --> 00:04:38,892
Many apprentices start at a percentage of

129
00:04:38,892 --> 00:04:40,189
a journeyman's wage,

130
00:04:40,189 --> 00:04:43,173
often somewhere around forty to fifty percent,

131
00:04:43,173 --> 00:04:45,184
and get raises every year or so

132
00:04:45,184 --> 00:04:46,287
as they progress.

133
00:04:46,467 --> 00:04:48,432
By the end of the apprenticeship,

134
00:04:48,432 --> 00:04:50,099
they're earning a full wage,

135
00:04:50,099 --> 00:04:52,540
with years of experience already on their

136
00:04:52,540 --> 00:04:52,957
resume.

137
00:04:53,307 --> 00:04:55,834
Compare that with a typical four year

138
00:04:55,834 --> 00:04:58,567
college student, who often pays tuition,

139
00:04:58,567 --> 00:05:00,822
may work part time for low wages,

140
00:05:00,822 --> 00:05:03,282
and graduates with no guarantee of a

141
00:05:03,282 --> 00:05:04,580
job in their field.

142
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:07,691
The apprentice finishes training with income,

143
00:05:07,691 --> 00:05:10,100
experience and usually far less debt.

144
00:05:10,451 --> 00:05:11,298
In real life.

145
00:05:11,478 --> 00:05:14,083
A nineteen year old plumbing apprentice might

146
00:05:14,083 --> 00:05:16,457
earn around eighteen to twenty dollars an

147
00:05:16,457 --> 00:05:17,789
hour in the first year,

148
00:05:17,789 --> 00:05:19,063
